{title: 275 - O God of Light}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #275 • ATKINSON • 11.10.11.10.}
{lyricist: Sarah E. Taylor}
{composer: H. Barrie Cabena}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 275}
{meta: tune ATKINSON}
{meta: meter 11.10.11.10.}
{meta: category Holy Scriptures - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]O [Bm]God [G]of light, [D]Your Word, [Am]a [Bm]lamp [G]unfailing,
[D]Shall [Bm]pierce [G]the darkness [C]of [Bm]our [G]earthbound [Am]way
[G]And [Em]show [F#dim]your [Bm]grace, [D]Your [Em]plan [F#dim]for [G]us [Em]unveiling,
[C]And [D]guide [Bm]our [Am]footsteps [F#dim]to [Bm]the [Am]perfect day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]From [Bm]days [G]of old,through [D]blind [Am]and [Bm]willful [C]ages,
[D]Though [Bm]we [G]rebelled, You [C]gently [G]sought again,
[G]And [Em]spoke [F#dim]through [Bm]saints, [D]apostles, [G]prophets, [D]sages,
[C]Who [D]wrote [Bm]with [Am]eager [F#dim]or [Bm]reluctant [Am]pen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Undimmed [G]by time,those words [Am]are [Bm]still [G]revealing
[D]To [Bm]sinful [G/D]hearts Your [C]justice [G]and Your [Am]grace;
[G]And [Em]questing [Bm]mortals [Em]longing [G]for [Em]Your [D]healing,
[C]See [D]Your [Bm]compassion [F#dim]in [Bm]the [Am]Savior's face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]To [Bm]all [G]the world [D]Your summons [Bm]You [G]are [C]sending,
[D]Through [Bm]all [G]the earth, to [C]every [G]land [Am]and [G]race,
[G]That myriad [F#dim]tongues, [D]in [Em]one [F#dim]great [G]anthem [D]blending,
[C]May [D]praise [Bm]and [Am]celebrate [Bm]Your [Am]gift [G]of [Am]grace.
{end_of_verse}
